# Risk Register

| Risk ID | Asset | Threat | Vulnerability | Likelihood (1-5) | Impact (1-5) | Risk Score | Existing Control | Recommended Control |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| R-001 | AD Domain Controller | Credential theft | Weak password policy for admins | 4 | 5 | 20 | Standard password policy | Enforce MFA on all privileged accounts |
| R-002 | EHR Database | Unauthorized access | Over-provisioned user roles | 3 | 5 | 15 | RBAC partially implemented | Quarterly access reviews |
| R-003 | Employee Accounts | Insider threat | Delayed account deprovisioning | 3 | 4 | 12 | Manual process by HR/IT | Automated IAM deprovisioning workflow |
| R-004 | PHI Data at Rest | Data breach | Unencrypted database backups | 2 | 5 | 10 | None | Enable AES-256 encryption on backups |
| R-005 | Remote Access | Network intrusion | No VPN requirement for remote access | 4 | 4 | 16 | None | Enforce VPN for all remote connections |

* Risk Score = Likelihood x Impact (Scale: 1-25)*
* Risk Levels: 1-6 (Low), 8-12 (Medium), 15-25 (High)*
